From 4d6c1895060291d81f493618855fb1d577820109 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HeDo <ldileo@digipa.it>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:12:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] plylib refuses an "element" header line that has no count

After reading the name of an element, the check of the count tested the name again (already
known not to be null) instead of the count, so a header that ends inside the line "element vertex"
passed a null pointer to atoi and crashed. It is now a syntax error like the missing name before it.
---
 wrap/ply/plylib.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wrap/ply/plylib.cpp b/wrap/ply/plylib.cpp
index a0e46593b..715e3a572 100644
--- a/wrap/ply/plylib.cpp
+++ b/wrap/ply/plylib.cpp
@@ -1233,7 +1233,7 @@ int PlyFile::OpenRead( const char * filename )
 #else
       token = strtok_r(0,SEP,&tokenPtr);
 #endif
-			if(name==0)
+			if(token==0)
 			{
 				error = E_SYNTAX;
 				goto error;
